scaler first     0.527 +- 0.063
scaler inside    0.536 +- 0.060
selector first   0.872 +- 0.046
selector inside  0.515 +- 0.082
mean shift of a column mean when the 12 test rows are left out, in sd units: 0.052 (theory sqrt(12/(60*48)) = 0.065)
largest chance correlation sqrt(2 ln(2p)/n) = 0.526
ln C(2000,10) = 60.9 nats of choice in the selector; the scaler makes none

== Q2: one StandardScaler object in two pipelines
pipeline A fitted on data 1: accuracy 0.990, scaler mean 0.07
pipeline B fitted on data 2: accuracy 0.990, scaler mean 99.36
pipeline A again on data 1:   accuracy 0.470   (same scaler object: A[0] is B[0] = True)
with clone(sc) for each pipeline: A 0.990, B 0.990, means 0.07 and 99.36
with memory: the pipeline holds a clone, the object passed in is unfitted: has mean_ = False; pipeline's own scaler has mean_ = True; same object = False

== Q3: a new column arrives at transform
remainder='drop'        : fitted on 4 columns, new table has 5 -> output shape (300, 11), no warning
remainder='drop'        : new column inserted in the middle -> output shape (300, 11)
remainder='passthrough' : fitted on 4 columns, new table has 5 -> output shape (300, 12), no warning
remainder='passthrough' : new column inserted in the middle -> output shape (300, 12)
remainder='drop'        : same, but plain arrays -> ValueError: X has 5 features, but ColumnTransformer is expecting 4 features as input.
remainder='passthrough' : same, but plain arrays -> ValueError: X has 5 features, but ColumnTransformer is expecting 4 features as input.
at fit, remainder='passthrough' on the full 6-column table keeps the other 3 columns: output width 14
plain arrays, passthrough: ValueError X has 5 features, but ColumnTransformer is expecting 4 features as input.

== Q4: totals and typical prices after a log target (sigma = 0.6)
total of the true prices 2723157; sum of median predictions 2275938 (16.4 per cent low); smeared 2724760 (0.06 per cent off)
smearing factor 1.1972, exp(sigma^2/2) = 1.1972
typical price: share of true prices below the median prediction 0.501, below the smeared one 0.618
mean absolute error: median 6.144, smeared 6.420; mean squared error: median 121.7, smeared 114.6
